Spec: InstanceMacros

Purpose:
  Generate, through six `#[macro_export]` declarative macros, the shared status-tracking
    surface injected into a Vynil instance CRD type: the @ApplicationCondition constructor
    families for install stages, the CRUD lookups, the condition-rebuilt @kube::api::Patch::Merge
    status patches with their Kubernetes events, and synchronous Rhai bridges over every
    mutator. Each instance module (./instanceservice.rs, ./instancesystem.rs,
    ./instancetenant.rs) expands the macros against its own local condition types; this spec
    freezes what one expansion does for a CRD type.

Owns:
  ./instance_macros.rs

References:
  ./instanceservice.rs, ./instancesystem.rs, ./instancetenant.rs — the only call sites, each
    expanding its subset of the macros at module scope (these modules depend on this file, not
    the reverse).
  ./instancesystem.sdd, ./ttl_cache.sdd — approved calibration references.

Must:
  Each macro carries `#[macro_export]`, placing it at the `common` crate root, and ./lib.rs
    declares this module with `#[macro_use]`, which also makes every macro text-visible to
    sibling `./src` modules without imports; all current expansions stay inside the `common` crate.
  Each condition macro injects one fresh `impl ApplicationCondition { ... }` item block resolved
    against the call-site module's @ApplicationCondition, @ConditionsStatus and
    @ConditionsType identifiers, which macro_rules does not hygienize; a second expansion
    targeting the same type in one module collides on fixed method names and is a compile
    error, so each module expands each macro at most once and must declare every
    @ConditionsType variant its expanded macros name.
  @impl_condition_children! and @impl_condition_crds! route every generated constructor through
    the @ApplicationCondition::new generated by @impl_condition_common!, so expanding them
    without @impl_condition_common! compiles only when the call site provides an equivalent
    in-file `new`.
  Every generated constructor funnels through @new, which stamps `last_transition_time` as
    @Some(@chrono::Utc::now()) — qualified `::chrono`, not call-site — and passes `message`,
    `status`, `condition_type` and the caller-supplied `generation` through unchanged.
  Every generated method that stamps conditions reads `metadata.generation` and records `1`
    when the field is @None, on every one of the three instance types.
  Every generated mutator rebuilds `conditions` through @get_conditions_excluding: stored
    conditions whose type appears in the exclude list are dropped, every other record is
    carried over byte-identical (timestamp included), and an absent status yields an empty
    base instead of failing.
  @patch_status sends the status subresource as a @kube::api::Patch::Merge carrying
    `apiVersion` `vynil.solidite.fr/v1` — a literal fixed in the macro, independent of
    `$kind_str` — `kind` set to the call-site `$kind_str` literal, and `status` set to the
    caller's JSON; it targets the namespaced @kube::api::Api for
    `@kube::ResourceExt::namespace().unwrap()`, resource name
    `self.metadata.name.clone().unwrap()`, with the server-side field manager from
    @crate::context::get_short_name(), and returns the server-merged object as @crate::Result<Self>.
  The status JSON keys ever written are exactly the literals `conditions`, `tfstate`,
    `rhaistate`, `tag`, `digest`, `services`, `befores`, `vitals`, `scalables`, `others`,
    `posts` and `crds`; they must match the serde field names of the consumer status struct.
  After a successful patch each mutator publishes its event through @send_event and returns the
    server reply, never the local object; a failed patch returns @Err before any event, and a
    publish failure that is not a @kube::Error::Api discards the successful patch result and
    returns @Err(@crate::Error::KubeError(..)).
  @send_event records against `self.object_ref(&())` with a @kube::runtime::events::Recorder
    built from the passed client and @crate::context::get_reporter(); every @kube::Error::Api
    publish failure ends as `Ok(())`, and the `tracing::warn!` runs unless the status message
    contains both `unable to create new content in namespace` and `being terminated`.
  The shared failure pattern (tofu, rhai, before, vital, scalable, other, post, init, schedule
    and crd failure setters) excludes `@ConditionsType::AgentStarted`, the stage type and
    `@ConditionsType::Installed`, appends the `stage_ko(reason)` and @ApplicationCondition::installed_ko
    both carrying the full reason, and appends @ApplicationCondition::ready_ko only when no
    surviving condition has type @ConditionsType::Ready — matched by type alone, ignoring
    generation and @ConditionsStatus.
  The shared stage-success pattern (befores, vitals, scalables, others, posts, crds) excludes
    only its own stage type, appends the fixed-message `stage_ok`, patches `conditions` plus the
    stage children key, and publishes a `Normal` event whose note counts the input list.
  @set_agent_started, @set_missing_box, @set_missing_package, @set_missing_requirement and
    @set_missing_init_version pass an @have_condition gate — full equality on condition type,
    generation, status and message — and on a hit return `Ok(self.clone())` with neither patch
    nor event; the other mutators have no idempotence gate and re-stamp plus re-publish on
    every call.
  @agent_started, @missing_box, @missing_package and @missing_requirement all write
    @ConditionsType::AgentStarted, so each one's rebuild (exclude list `[AgentStarted]`) evicts
    the others' records.
  Warning-event notes are the reason string truncated in place with `@str::truncate(1023)`
    bytes; @ApplicationCondition messages stored in `conditions` keep the full untruncated
    reason; the `MissingJukebox`, `MissingPackage` and `InitVersionNotFound` notes are
    format-built strings and are not truncated.
  Every Rhai bridge over an async method drives its body through @tokio::task::block_in_place
    plus @tokio::runtime::Handle::block_on on @tokio::runtime::Handle::current — which panics on
    a current-thread runtime — and flattens any failure through @crate::rhai_err into an
    @rhai::EvalAltResult string, losing the @crate::Error variant; the purely synchronous bridges
    (@rhai_get_tfstate, @rhai_get_rhaistate, @get_metadata, @get_spec, @get_status) run inline
    without that bridge.
  Bridges taking a @rhai::Dynamic argument (@rhai_set_services, @rhai_set_status_befores,
    @rhai_set_status_vitals, @rhai_set_status_scalables, @rhai_set_status_others,
    @rhai_set_status_posts, @rhai_set_status_crds) convert it by a @serde_json string round-trip
    into `Vec<@crate::Published>`, `Vec<@crate::Children>` or `Vec<@String>`; a mis-shaped
    argument fails with a flattened @crate::Error::SerializationError before touching the cluster.
  @rhai_set_status_ready, generated by @impl_instance_common!, delegates to the `$type`'s
    @set_status_ready that the macro itself never defines — the expansion only compiles
    when @impl_instance_befores! is also expanded or the call site carries an in-file method,
    as ./instancesystem.rs does.
  @get_options_digest returns the @sha256::digest hex of the @serde_json serialization of
    `spec.options`, serializing with @Result::unwrap, or @sha256::digest of `""` when
    options are @None; @set_status_ready computes it over `self.clone()` because the method
    takes `&mut self` without mutating.
  @get_metadata, @get_spec and @get_status convert `metadata`, `spec` and `status` to
    @rhai::Dynamic by a @serde_json to-string-then-from-string double step, each leg mapped to
    a flattened @crate::Error::SerializationError; a @None status surfaces as Rhai null.
  Expansion names resolve in call-site-crate scope for the unqualified `sha256`, `serde_json`
    and `tracing` paths and for the @kube::ResourceExt trait import behind `namespace()` and
    `object_ref()`, while `$crate::tools::encode_base64_gz` and
    `$crate::tools::base64_gz_decode` address a private module — the macros therefore only
    expand inside the `common` crate today.

Depends on:
  @kube::api::Api, @kube::api::ListParams, @kube::api::Patch, @kube::api::PatchParams and
    @kube::Client — namespaced lookups and the status-subresource merge patch.
  @kube::runtime::events::Recorder, @kube::runtime::events::Event and
    @kube::runtime::events::EventType — event publication against the instance object ref.
  @crate::context::get_client_async, @crate::context::get_short_name and
    @crate::context::get_reporter in ./context.rs — per-call client (which panics when no
    @kube::Client can be built), patch field manager, event reporter.
  @crate::tools::encode_base64_gz and @crate::tools::base64_gz_decode in ./tools.rs — the
    base64+gzip codec for tfstate/rhaistate, propagating their @crate::Error variants.
  @crate::Error, @crate::Result, @crate::RhaiRes and @crate::rhai_err in ./lib.rs — the
    error contract propagated by async setters and flattened at Rhai bridges.
  @crate::Children and @crate::Published in ./lib.rs — child inventory and published-service
    records stored through the stage and services setters.
  @kube::ResourceExt — trait whose `namespace()` and `object_ref()` calls in expanded code must
    be imported at each call site; @kube::Resource — the @kube::api::Api bound on `$type`,
    satisfied by the CustomResource derive.
  @sha256::digest, @serde_json and @tracing — resolved against call-site-crate scope, not
    `$crate`; see the hygiene task below.
  @chrono::Utc::now — condition timestamps (qualified `::chrono` in the expansion).
  @tokio::task::block_in_place and @tokio::runtime::Handle — sync-to-async bridge under every
    Rhai mutator bridge.
  @rhai::Dynamic — the argument type accepted from package scripts.

Exposes:
  @impl_condition_common! — no-arg, module-scope; injects thirteen @ApplicationCondition
    constructors — @new plus twelve fixed-shape presets routing through it:
    @new(message, status, condition_type, generation) with
    `#[must_use]`; @ready_ok(generation) `True`/`Ready`/`Installed succesfully`;
    @ready_ko(generation) `False`/`Ready`/`No successful install`; @installed_ko(message, generation)
    `False`/`Installed`/caller message; @installed_ok(generation) `True`/`Installed`/`Installed
    succesfully`; @agent_started(generation) `True`/`AgentStarted`/`Agent started`;
    @missing_package(cat, name, generation) `False`/`AgentStarted`/`Package {cat}/{name} is missing`;
    @missing_box(name, generation) `False`/`AgentStarted`/`JukeBox {name} is missing`;
    @missing_requirement(error, generation) `False`/`AgentStarted`/caller error;
    @tofu_ko(message, generation) `False`/`TofuInstalled`; @tofu_ok(generation)
    `True`/`TofuInstalled`/`Tofu layer applied succesfully`; @rhai_ko(message, generation)
    `False`/`RhaiApplied`; @rhai_ok(generation) `True`/`RhaiApplied`/`Custom rhai script succeed`.
  @impl_condition_children! — no-arg; injects thirteen constructors over the children-stage
    types, all through @new: @vital_ko(message, generation) `False`/`VitalApplied`;
    @vital_ok(generation) `True`/`VitalApplied`/`vitals templates applied succesfully`;
    @before_ko(message, generation) `False`/`BeforeApplied`; @before_ok(generation)
    `True`/`BeforeApplied`/`befores templates applied succesfully`; @scalable_ko(message, generation)
    `False`/`ScalableApplied`; @scalable_ok(generation) `True`/`ScalableApplied`/`Scalables
    templates applied succesfully`; @post_ko(message, generation) `False`/`PostApplied`;
    @post_ok(generation) `True`/`PostApplied`/`Templates applied succesfully`;
    @other_ko(message, generation) `False`/`OtherApplied`; @other_ok(generation)
    `True`/`OtherApplied`/`Templates applied succesfully`; @init_ko(message, generation)
    `False`/`InitFrom`; @init_version_ko(version, generation) `False`/`InitFrom`/
    `[E_INIT_VERSION_NOT_FOUND] Version {version} introuvable dans le registre OCI`;
    @schedule_ko(message, generation) `False`/`ScheduleBackup`.
  @impl_condition_crds! — no-arg; injects @crd_ko(message, generation) `False`/`CrdApplied` and
    @crd_ok(generation) `True`/`CrdApplied`/`CRD(s) applied succesfully`.
  @impl_instance_common!($type, $kind_str) — injects into `$type` the shared surface:
    async @get(namespace, name) namespaced lookup; async @list(namespace) with
    @kube::api::ListParams::default; @get_options_digest sync digest (Must section);
    @get_tfstate and @get_rhaistate sync base64+gzip decode, `Ok(@None)` when no status or no
    stored state; private @have_condition(cond) full four-field equality probe used by the
    gates; private @get_conditions_excluding(exclude) rebuild; private @patch_status(client,
    patch) merge-patch per the Must section; private @send_event(client, event) per the Must
    section; async @set_tfstate(tfstate) excludes `TofuInstalled`, appends @tofu_ok, patches
    `conditions` + `tfstate` (gzip-encoded), then `Normal` reason `TofuApplySucceed` action
    `TofuApply` without note; async @set_status_tofu_failed(tfstate, reason) failure pattern
    over `TofuInstalled`, patches `conditions` + `tfstate`, `Warning` `TofuApplyFailed`/
    `TofuApply` with note = truncated reason; async @set_rhaistate(rhaistate) excludes
    `RhaiApplied`, appends @rhai_ok, patches `conditions` + `rhaistate`, `Normal`
    `RhaiApplySucceed`/`RhaiApply`; async @set_status_rhai_failed(rhaistate, reason) failure
    pattern over `RhaiApplied`, patches `conditions` + `rhaistate`, `Warning`
    `RhaiApplyFailed`/`RhaiApply` truncated note; async @set_agent_started gated, excludes
    `AgentStarted`, `Normal` `AgentStarted`/`AgentStart` no note; async @set_missing_box(jukebox)
    gated, excludes `AgentStarted`, `Warning` `MissingJukebox`/`AgentStart` note
    `JukeBox {jukebox} doesnt exist`; async @set_missing_package(category, package) gated,
    excludes `AgentStarted`, `Warning` `MissingPackage`/`AgentStart` note
    `Package {category}/{package} doesnt exist`; async @set_missing_requirement(reason) gated,
    excludes `AgentStarted`, `Warning` `MissingRequirement`/`AgentStart` truncated note.
    Rhai bridges: @rhai_get(namespace, name); @rhai_list(namespace) collecting the
    @kube::api::ObjectList into @Vec; @get_metadata, @get_spec, @get_status (Dynamic round-trips);
    @rhai_get_tfstate and @rhai_get_rhaistate defaulting `@None` to `""` and running synchronously;
    @rhai_set_status_ready(tag); @rhai_set_tfstate(tfstate); @rhai_set_status_tofu_failed(tfstate,
    reason); @rhai_set_rhaistate(rhaistate); @rhai_set_status_rhai_failed(rhaistate, reason);
    @rhai_set_agent_started; @rhai_set_missing_box(jukebox); @rhai_set_missing_package(category,
    package); @rhai_set_missing_requirement(reason).
  @impl_instance_befores!($type) — injects into `$type` the children-management surface:
    async @set_status_ready(tag) excludes `AgentStarted`, `BeforeApplied`, `Ready`, `Installed`,
    `InitFrom` and `ScheduleBackup`, appends @ready_ok + @installed_ok, patches `conditions` +
    `tag` + `digest` (clone-computed options digest), `Normal` `InstallSucceed`/`Install`;
    @get_services sync status `services` list defaulting to empty; @get_services_string sync
    sorted service `key` values joined on the literal `,`, or `""` when absent;
    async @set_services(services) patches `services` only, no conditions, no event; async
    @set_status_befores(befores), @set_status_vitals(vitals), @set_status_scalables(scalables),
    @set_status_others(others), @set_status_posts(posts) each stage-success over
    `BeforeApplied`, `VitalApplied`, `ScalableApplied`, `OtherApplied`, `PostApplied` patching
    `conditions` + `befores`/`vitals`/`scalables`/`others`/`posts` with `Normal` reasons
    `BeforeApplySucceed`, `VitalApplySucceed`, `ScalableApplySucceed`, `OtherApplySucceed`,
    `PostApplySucceed`, actions `BeforeApply`, `VitalApply`, `ScalableApply`, `OtherApply`,
    `PostApply`, and note `Applied {count} Objects`; async @set_status_before_failed,
    @set_status_vital_failed, @set_status_scalable_failed, @set_status_other_failed and
    @set_status_post_failed each failure pattern over its stage type, `Warning` reasons
    `BeforeApplyFailed`, `VitalApplyFailed`, `ScalableApplyFailed`, `OtherApplyFailed` and —
    verbatim from the others stage — `OtherApplyFailed` for posts, with actions mirroring the
    success actions (`OtherApply` for posts) and truncated notes; async @set_status_init_failed(reason)
    failure pattern over `InitFrom`, `Warning` `InitFromFail`/`InitFrom` truncated note; async
    @set_status_schedule_backup_failed(reason) failure pattern over `ScheduleBackup`, `Warning`
    `ScheduleBackupFailed`/`ScheduleBackup` truncated note; async @set_missing_init_version(version)
    gated, excludes only `InitFrom` with no `installed_ko`/`ready_ko` appends, `Warning`
    `InitVersionNotFound`/`InitFrom` whose note repeats the condition message.
    Rhai bridges: @rhai_set_services(list) @rhai::Dynamic-converted; @rhai_get_services returning
    @String directly with no @crate::RhaiRes; @rhai_set_status_befores, @rhai_set_status_before_failed,
    @rhai_set_status_vitals, @rhai_set_status_vital_failed, @rhai_set_status_scalables,
    @rhai_set_status_scalable_failed, @rhai_set_status_others, @rhai_set_status_other_failed,
    @rhai_set_status_posts, @rhai_set_status_post_failed, @rhai_set_status_init_failed,
    @rhai_set_status_schedule_backup_failed and @rhai_set_missing_init_version, each bridging its
    async twin.
  @impl_instance_crds!($type) — injects async @set_status_crds(crds) stage-success over
    `CrdApplied` patching `conditions` + `crds` with `Normal` reason `CRDApplySucceed`, action
    `CRDApply`, note `Applied {count} CustomResourceDefinition`; async @set_status_crd_failed(reason)
    failure pattern over `CrdApplied` with `Warning` `CRDApplyFailed`/`CRDApply` truncated note;
    Rhai bridges @rhai_set_status_crds(list) @rhai::Dynamic-converted to `@Vec<@String>` and
    @rhai_set_status_crd_failed(reason).

Accepts:
  @impl_condition_common!, @impl_condition_children! and @impl_condition_crds! accept no
    fragments and must be invoked at module scope (the expansion is an `impl` item, not valid
    inside an `impl` block).
  @impl_instance_common! accepts a `$type:ty` fragment plus a `$kind_str:literal` fragment; the
    literal is embedded verbatim as the patch `kind`, so correctness requires the CRD kind
    string (`ServiceInstance`, `TenantInstance`, `SystemInstance` at current call sites) and the
    macro cannot retarget the group/version.
  @impl_instance_befores! and @impl_instance_crds! accept only `$type:ty`.
  The target `$type` must expose `spec` with an @Option `options` JSON map (digest, @get_spec),
    a kube-derived `metadata` @kube::api::ObjectMeta with `generation` and `name`, and an
    @Option `status` carrying `conditions` always, `tfstate`/`rhaistate` for the common macro,
    `services`/`befores`/`vitals`/`scalables`/`others`/`posts` for the befores macro, and `crds`
    for the crds macro; the type must be @Clone and serde-@Serialize/@Deserialize.
  Generated method arguments are unvalidated free-form strings — `namespace`, `name`, `tag`,
    `reason`, `version`, `category`, `package`, `jukebox` — and opaque state strings, which the
    setters must be able to gzip+base64-encode.

Returns:
  Expansions return nothing at runtime — they inject impl blocks at compile time.
  Async mutators return @crate::Result<Self> whose `Ok` carries the server-merged object read
    back from @patch_status; gated setters return `Ok(self.clone())` unchanged on a gate hit.
  @get returns @crate::Result<Self>, @list @crate::Result<@kube::api::ObjectList<Self>>,
    @get_tfstate and @get_rhaistate @crate::Result<@Option<@String>>.
  @get_options_digest returns the hex digest @String; @get_services a @Vec<@crate::Published>;
    @get_services_string the joined keys or `""`.
  Rhai bridges return @crate::RhaiRes over the same payloads (@rhai_list a @Vec<Self>, the
    json accessors @rhai::Dynamic), except @rhai_get_services which returns @String.

Raises:
  @crate::Error::KubeError from @get, @list and @patch_status when any Kubernetes call fails,
    and from @send_event for every @kube::Error variant other than `Api`.
  The base64/gzip codec errors (@crate::Error::Base64DecodeError, @crate::Error::Stdio) from
    @crate::tools in @get_tfstate, @get_rhaistate, @set_tfstate, @set_rhaistate and the two combined
    failure setters.
  @crate::Error::SerializationError (pre-flattening) when a Rhai @rhai::Dynamic argument or a
    `metadata`/`spec`/`status` round-trip fails; every Rhai bridge hands it to @crate::rhai_err
    so the caller sees only the message text in an @rhai::EvalAltResult.
  Panics: `@str::truncate(1023)` when the byte falls inside a multi-byte character; the
    @Option::unwrap calls in @patch_status when namespace or name is absent and the
    @Result::unwrap in @get_options_digest on serialization; @tokio::task::block_in_place on a
    current-thread runtime; and @crate::context::get_client_async (upstream) when no client can
    be built.

Handles:
  Gate setter whose exact condition (type + generation + status + message) is already stored —
    returns the clone with no patch and no event.
  A surviving `Ready`-type condition at any generation or status during a failure pattern — it
    is carried through and no @ready_ko is appended.
  Status absent or `conditions` empty — the rebuild starts from nothing.
  `metadata.generation` absent — stamped `1`.
  `spec.options` @None — @get_options_digest still returns the digest of `""`.
  No stored tfstate/rhaistate — `Ok(@None)`, or `""` through the Rhai getters.
  Event publish failing with a @kube::Error::Api — swallowed to `Ok(())`; logged via
    `tracing::warn!` unless the message carries both terminating-namespace phrases.
  Reason longer than 1023 bytes — event note truncated, stored condition message kept whole.

Tasks:
  [ ] No @tests module exists in this file. The only mapped coverage is
      @test_init_version_ko_message_contains_error_id_and_version and
      @test_have_condition_detects_init_version_ko in ./instancetenant.rs, which exercise the
      generated @init_version_ko and the private @have_condition probe; no test covers the
      patched outputs, gates, events or Rhai bridges. Cover the Scenario blocks from consumer
      @tests modules under the TTD rule when test work starts.
  [?] @get_options_digest serializes options via @Result::unwrap — practically unreachable for a
      JSON map, yet it is an @unwrap call in product code, kept invisible because the
      static-analysis harness in /linting.sdd does not lint inside macro expansions. Decide
      later whether to propagate or keep.
  [?] @patch_status @Option::unwrap calls on `@kube::ResourceExt::namespace()` and `metadata.name` panic
      locally for a client-side-built object without namespace or name. Decide later whether a
      typed error is required.
  [?] Failure notes and requirement notes truncate by byte index with `@str::truncate(1023)`,
      which panics when `1023` falls inside a multi-byte character of a non-ASCII reason, while
      the condition `message` stays untruncated. Decide later whether truncation must be
      char-safe.
  [?] @send_event turns every @kube::Error::Api into `Ok(())`; the De Morgan guard
      `!contains(..) || !contains(..)` only decides whether `tracing::warn!` fires (silent only
      when both phrases appear). Failing to publish an event is therefore invisible to callers
      by default. Decide later whether non-terminating-namespace publish failures must
      propagate.
  [?] @set_status_post_failed emits `Warning` reason `OtherApplyFailed` action `OtherApply`
      while recording `PostApplied` conditions — a copy from the others stage; observers and
      event consumers misattribute post failures. Freeze kept; decide whether the strings may
      change.
  [?] The failure-pattern @ready_ko check matches surviving conditions on @ConditionsType::Ready
      type alone, so a `Ready`/`True` from an older generation suppresses the failure's ready
      marking. The same finding is recorded in ./instancesystem.sdd for its in-file setter;
      decide later whether generation or status must be considered.
  [?] Stage-success setters (@set_tfstate, @set_rhaistate, @set_status_ready, the five child
      stages, @set_status_crds, @set_services) carry no idempotence gate — every call
      re-stamps @chrono::Utc::now timestamps, rewrites the keys and re-publishes events. Decide
      whether the @have_condition pattern must be generalized.
  [?] @agent_started, @missing_box, @missing_package and @missing_requirement share
      @ConditionsType::AgentStarted, so each write evicts the others and the `AgentStarted`
      trace cannot show which is missing alongside another. Confirm the sharing is intended.
  [?] Wire-visible strings frozen as-is: misspelled `succesfully` in most ok-messages,
      `doesnt exist` in event notes, `Custom rhai script succeed`, lowercase `vitals`/`befores`
      prefixes, the identical `Templates applied succesfully` on @post_ok and @other_ok, and the
      French-only `[E_INIT_VERSION_NOT_FOUND] Version {version} introuvable dans le registre OCI`
      (identifier matches the root spec error-identity rule). Decide later whether corrected
      strings are acceptable CRD-visible changes.
  [?] Doc-comment drift: @get_metadata, @get_spec and @get_status document
      `Error::KubeError when the Kubernetes API call fails` although they perform no API call;
      the @impl_condition_children! doc omits `PostApplied` from its covered list; the
      @impl_instance_befores! doc names only three of the six @set_status_ready exclusions; and
      the @impl_instance_common! doc demands call-site imports (@kube::api::ObjectList,
      @kube::api::Patch, @kube::api::PatchParams) while the fully-qualified `::kube::...`
      expansion needs only the @kube::ResourceExt trait import for `namespace()`/`object_ref()`.
      Rewrite wordings later.
  [?] Hygiene portability: the `#[macro_export]` surface promises cross-crate reuse, but
      unqualified `sha256`, `serde_json`, `tracing` and the private `$crate::tools` mean an
      expansion only compiles inside `common`; ./lib.rs also declares this module
      `#[macro_use] pub`, giving every macro two import paths. Decide whether to
      qualify these paths and stabilize one export path, or to document the in-crate-only
      contract.
  [?] @impl_instance_common! is not standalone: `@rhai_set_status_ready` references
      the `$type`'s @set_status_ready that @impl_instance_befores! or an in-file method must provide
      (./instancesystem.rs does). Decide whether to fold, parameterize, or document the
      coupling.
  [?] @rhai_get_services returns @String instead of @crate::RhaiRes and wraps a purely
      synchronous call in @tokio::task::block_in_place plus @tokio::runtime::Handle::block_on,
      so it still panics on a current-thread runtime without awaiting anything. Decide later
      whether the bridge shape changes.
  [?] @set_missing_init_version diverges from the sibling failure setters: it gates, excludes
      only `InitFrom`, never appends @installed_ko/@ready_ko, and repeats the condition message
      verbatim as event note. Confirm the asymmetry against the install flow is intended.
  [?] @get_options_digest takes `&mut self` while only reading — the `&mut` exists to fit Rhai
      `register_fn` accessor registration as used by all three consumer registers. Decide
      whether an immutable signature with a registration-side adapter is wanted.
  [?] The runtime assumption that every Rhai bridge host runs a `multi-thread` @tokio runtime
      is nowhere enforced; already recorded per-consumer in ./instancesystem.sdd. Decide once,
      centrally, whether to enforce or redesign the bridges.

Done when:
  Every Scenario above has a passing mapped test in a consumer @tests module and
    `cargo test -p common` is green.

Scenario: Stamped constructor shape
  Given a module that expanded @impl_condition_common!, such as ./instancesystem.rs
  When @tofu_ok is called with generation `4`
  Then the record is `True`/`TofuInstalled` with message `Tofu layer applied succesfully`
    and generation `4`
  And `last_transition_time` is @Some(@chrono::Utc::now) captured at construction
  No mapped test exists for this Scenario yet; see the open task above.

Scenario: Init-version failure message carries the error identifier
  Given ./instancetenant.rs expanded @impl_condition_common! and @impl_condition_children!
  When @init_version_ko is called with version `1.5.0` and generation `3`
  Then the record is `False`/`InitFrom` with message
    `[E_INIT_VERSION_NOT_FOUND] Version 1.5.0 introuvable dans le registre OCI` and generation `3`
  Maps to test @test_init_version_ko_message_contains_error_id_and_version

Scenario: Gate hit skips patch and event
  Given an instance whose stored conditions already contain the exact record @init_version_ko
    would build, matched on type, generation, status and message by @have_condition
  When @set_missing_init_version is awaited with the same version and generation
  Then the setter returns `Ok(self.clone())`, patches nothing and publishes no event
  @test_have_condition_detects_init_version_ko covers the @have_condition probe only; the
    gated early return of the setter itself has no test yet.

Scenario: Tofu failure without a Ready condition marks three stages
  Given an instance at absent `metadata.generation` whose status holds a stale
    `TofuInstalled`/`False`, an `AgentStarted`/`True` and a `CrdApplied`/`True` record
  When @set_status_tofu_failed is awaited with state string `x` and reason `boom`
  Then the patched `conditions` are the carried `CrdApplied` record plus `TofuInstalled`/`False`
    and `Installed`/`False` with message `boom` and generation `1`, plus an appended
    `Ready`/`False` with message `No successful install`
  And the patch carries `tfstate` set to the gzip+base64 encoding of `x`
  And a `Warning` event reason `TofuApplyFailed` action `TofuApply` note `boom` is published
  And every `AgentStarted` record is dropped
  No mapped test exists for this Scenario yet.

Scenario: Stale-generation Ready survives a macro-driven failure
  Given an instance at `metadata.generation` `4` whose status holds a `Ready`/`True` record
    from generation `3`
  When @set_status_rhai_failed is awaited with any state and reason
  Then no @ApplicationCondition::ready_ko is appended and the generation-`3` `Ready`/`True`
    record is carried through, so the printed Ready column still reports the older success
    while `Installed` flips to `False`
  No mapped test exists for this Scenario yet.

Scenario: Children-stage ready close rewrites exclusions, tag and digest
  Given a @ServiceInstance whose status holds `TofuInstalled`/`True`, `RhaiApplied`/`False`,
    a stale `BeforeApplied`, an `AgentStarted`, an `InitFrom` and a `ScheduleBackup` record
  When @set_status_ready is awaited with tag `1.2.3`
  Then the patched `conditions` keep only the `TofuInstalled` and `RhaiApplied` records plus
    fresh `Ready` and `Installed` conditions at the current generation
  And the patch carries `tag` `1.2.3` and a `digest` equal to @get_options_digest for the same
    spec options
  And a `Normal` event reason `InstallSucceed` action `Install` is published
  No mapped test exists for this Scenario yet.

Scenario: Absent options still produces a digest
  Given a @ServiceInstance whose `spec.options` is @None
  When @set_status_ready is awaited
  Then the patched `digest` is the @sha256::digest of the empty string
  No mapped test exists for this Scenario yet.

Scenario: Mis-shaped Rhai list is rejected before any patch
  Given a package script calling the registered crds setter with a @rhai::Dynamic whose JSON
    cannot deserialize to `@Vec<@String>`
  When @rhai_set_status_crds runs
  Then the call returns an @rhai::EvalAltResult carrying the serialized
    @crate::Error::SerializationError message
  And no status patch or event is attempted
  No mapped test exists for this Scenario yet.

Scenario: Api event failure is swallowed
  Given an awaited mutator whose status patch succeeded but whose event publish fails with a
    @kube::Error::Api status
  Then the mutator still completes `Ok` with the server-merged object
  And the failure is recorded by `tracing::warn!` unless the status message contains both
    `unable to create new content in namespace` and `being terminated`
  No mapped test exists for this Scenario yet.
